// PRELUDE CONTRACT FOR THIS OPEN TRANCHE.
//
// Keep this file under Next while its syntax and semantics are unimplemented. During the Prelude
// implementation slice, teach the grammar, scoping, validator, formatter, compiler, and runtime
// these declarations, then replace `packages/stdlib/tao/Prelude.tao` with this contract as Current
// migrates. After focused package coverage and `./agent verify` pass, delete this `@tao-next`
// scratch package before closing the tranche and arming the Next/Current byte-identity gates.
//
// Core primitives are compiler-known types. A primitive without `is` is an opaque root; `is`
// declares a nominal refinement of another core type.

primitive item

primitive number

primitive text

primitive boolean

primitive list

primitive time

primitive action

primitive design

// Rendering and presentability are independent roles. Every presentable is visual, but an
// embeddable view, layout, or frame is not thereby directly presentable by a navigator.
primitive visual

primitive presentable is visual

primitive view is visual

// `layout` and `frame` intrinsically accept caller content and bind `@@content` in their render
// bodies. Content acceptance is a declaration-kind capability, not a declared property or slot.
primitive layout is visual

primitive frame is visual

primitive ui is presentable

primitive nav is presentable with {
   implement,
}

primitive datasource with {
   implement,
}

primitive app with {
   Name text,
   Navigator nav,
   Datasource datasource is none,
   Design design is none,
}
